"B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lindqvist</surname><given-names>&#x000c5;</given-names></name><name><surname>Ljungstr&#x000f6;m</surname><given-names>BL</given-names></name><name><surname>Nilsson</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Waller</surname><given-names>PJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The dynamics, prevalence and impact of nematode parasite infections in organically raised sheep in Sweden</article-title><source>Acta Vet Scand</source><year>2001</year><volume>42</volume><fpage>377</fpage><lpage>389</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11887398</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1186/1751-0147-42-377</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nilsson</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Rudby-Martin</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Schwan</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Bensimidazol-resistenta <italic>Haemonchus contortus </italic>p&#x000e5;visade hos f&#x000e5;r i Sverige (Benzimidazole resistance demonstrated in <italic>Haemonchus contortus </italic>infections of sheep in Sweden)</article-title><source>Sv Vet Tid</source><year>1993</year><volume>45</volume><fpage>303</fpage><lpage>307</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nyman</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Alternative methods of treating gastrointestinal nematodes in sheep, using <italic>Duddingtonia flagrans </italic>and copper wire particles. Minor Field Studies No. 99</article-title><source>Swedish University of Agricultural Sciences, International Office, Uppsala, Sweden</source><year>2000</year><fpage>54</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-gr