y response to natural infestation in grazing sheep and the "self cure" phenomenon</article-title><source>Aust J Agric Res</source><year>1950</year><volume>1</volume><fpage>427</fpage><lpage>439</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1071/AR9500427</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Waller</surname><given-names>PJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Rudby-Martin</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Ljungstr&#x000f6;m</surname><given-names>BL</given-names></name><name><surname>Rydzik</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The epidemiology of abomasal nematodes of sheep in Sweden, with particular reference to overwinter survival strategies</article-title><source>Vet Parasitol</source><year>2004</year><volume>122</volume><fpage>207</fpage><lpage>220</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15219362</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.vetpar.2004.04.007</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Watkins</surname><given-names>AD</given-names></name><name><surname>Miller</surname><given-names>JE</given-names></name><name><surname>Terrill</surname><given-names>TH</given-names></name><name><surname>Larsen</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Kaplan</surname><given-names>RM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Effectiveness of copper-oxide wire particles on the control of <italic>Haemonchus contortus </italic>in sheep</article-title><source>Proc 19th WAAVP Conference New Orleans</source><fpage>198</fpage><comment>August 10&#x02013;14, 2003</comment></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>